This chart and table demostrates information on the police budget for 2017 and 2018 in a area in UK, showing both how the money are earned and how it was used. This report will going through the difference between 2017 and 2018.

In 2017, police budget was mostly used in national government, using 175.5m pounds. Meanwhile, taxes provided 91.2m and 38m was rewarded by other sources, like grants. The money was spent 3 forth on salaries for staffs or officers, 8% on techonogy, and 17% on buildings and transport.

In 2018, police budget has increased by 13.9m, result in 177.8m on a national government. Local taxes, as well as other sources have become 102.3m and 38.5m. Meanwhile, there is 69% of money used in salaries. Police also used 14% on techonogy, instead of 8% in 2015. Both 2017 and the next year resulted in the same persentage on buldings and transport.

Overall, 2018 earned more money than 2017, used more money on techonogy.